# Home waters at dusk (#227): the lantern chattering on the bow pole while
# you row out to the buoy, as you've done a hundred times. Each section is
# tagged with the moment it's for; the scene (scripts/intro/home_waters.gd)
# says the moments as you go, each once, in the order they happen, waiting
# for the last to finish.
#
# Moments, roughly in the order they come:
#   left_jetty    you've pulled away from the jetty
#   out_quarter   a fifth of the way to the buoy
#   out_half      halfway
#   by_chain      you're passing beside the great chain
#   buoy_sighted  the buoy's near enough to see clearly
#   out_most      nearly there
#   at_buoy       you've come alongside
#   too_far       you've rowed off into the fog (said again, in turn, if you
#                 stay out there)
#
# First drafts: rewrite freely.

~ left_jetty [on left_jetty]
lantern: Off we go. Out to the buoy, light it, home for stew.
lantern: Mind the third post. You always nearly hit the third post.

~ out_quarter [on out_quarter]
lantern: Smell that? The onions are on already.

~ out_half [on out_half]
lantern: Halfway. I counted. I always count.
lantern: Ninety-one strokes, if you don't dawdle. You're dawdling.

~ by_chain [on by_chain]
lantern: Evening, chain.
lantern: It hums, you know. You'll feel it when we tie up. Like a cat, only iron.

~ buoy_sighted [on buoy_sighted]
lantern: There she is. Lamp's out again, look.
lantern: Don't worry. I've got plenty.

~ out_most [on out_most]
lantern: Easy on the last bit, or you'll bump her and she sulks.

~ at_buoy [on at_buoy]
lantern: Bump. ...Gently, I said.

~ too_far_1 [on too_far]
lantern: Wrong way, chain-tender. The buoy's back there.

~ too_far_2 [on too_far]
lantern: There's nothing out here but fog. Turn us round?
